					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE: INTERSECTING RECTANGLES\n\nIn this example we have two Rectangle geometries moving up, down, left and right.\nNext we convert the geometry to a mesh and the mesh to a texture.\nAt the same time we are also converting the mesh to a Box2D type by using the Bounding Box node.\nThis gives us the bounding box of the mesh.\n\nWe split the signal and check wheter the rectangles intersect.\nIf so, we Colorize the rectangles red, if not, it stays white."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 732.744384765625,
					"width": 2531.6826171875,
					"x": -590.68548583984375,
					"y": 75.82463836669921875
				},
